# Template. Copy to pmc-key.conf and point it at the real key.
#
# PLACEHOLDER ONLY. This file is generated by blanking the value, never by
# copying a working pmc-key.conf - a real path pasted into an example is how
# machine-specific detail reaches a public repository.
#
# pmc-key.conf is gitignored. It must be listed AFTER pmc.conf on the build
# command line so that this value overrides the fail-closed placeholder there;
# tools/build.ps1 does that, and refuses to build MCUboot if the file is
# absent.
#
# The key itself lives OUTSIDE every repository, in
# Documents/Arduino/mcuboot-signing/, and is per-project: a Giga image must not
# be installable on this board, nor the reverse. Generate with
#
#   imgtool keygen -k <dir>/pmc-explorer-ec-p256.pem -t ecdsa-p256
#
# BACK IT UP. Losing it means no future image can be signed for a board already
# carrying this bootloader, and the only way back is to reinstall MCUboot over
# BOOT0 + RST.
CONFIG_BOOT_SIGNATURE_KEY_FILE=""
